      ],
      "notes": [
        "The combat bowl: the default 20 x 14 with a 3 x 3 pillar standing in the middle of it, so the pillar is the only thing that differs from `TRAINING_OCTAGON`.",
        "The floor is a *ring* of four convex regions. Their union is the rectangle minus the central square, which is what makes the middle unwalkable — and that in turn is what lets the renderer stand a column there without breaking the decor invariant that nothing solid ever occupies playable floor. The outline stays the full rectangle because the floor really does continue under the column; it is a pillar, not a pit.",
        "3 units across is chosen against the reach numbers, not for looks: it is wider than the 2.4 heavy reach, so two bodies on opposite faces genuinely cannot touch each other. That is the whole question the room asks — whether a sightline break the player can round faster than a guard turns melee spacing into something with a second axis."
      ]
    },
